### the-construction
- The record above is now a construction: `chem/identity.cub`, 448 definitions checking, written over
  `lib/core.cub`. What each node of this document asserted informally is stated there as a type or proved
  there as a theorem, and nothing in it is a representation choice awaiting a schema.
- `Mol` is a molecule as the structured graph of its atoms — a type of atoms, each atom's element, each
  ordered pair's bond — with no numbering of the atoms part of the molecule. `Auto` is an automorphism:
  a relabelling carrying its inverse as data together with its preservation of element and bond, and
  `auto-id`, `auto-comp`, `auto-inv` are its group structure, each proved from that data and no further
  principle. This is the object `automorphism-is-physical` named and `canonicalization` showed the field
  computing and discarding.
- `Orbit` is the witnessed same-orbit relation, with `orbit-refl`, `orbit-sym`, `orbit-trans`, and
  `orbit-invariant` is the theorem: an observation of an atom invariant under the automorphisms is
  constant on orbits. That is what makes "chemically equivalent positions" a property of the molecule
  rather than of a drawing, and it is proved with no finiteness, no set-hood and no truncation — the
  witness carries the whole argument.
- `Taut` carries the tautomers as a type whose paths are the admissible proton transfers, `taut-rec` is
  its elimination, and `taut-respects` is the consequence that matters: any function out of it already
  respects every transfer. A tautomer-dependent quantity therefore cannot be stated of the substance at
  all, which is `tautomers`' problem turned from a defect of a digest into a property of the carrier.
- `digest-sound` holds of any digest whatever and is all that any hashing scheme establishes.
  `DigestInjective` is what would license reading identity off a string. `Collision` is two molecules not
  identical whose digests are, and `collision-not-injective` derives the refutation of injectivity from a
  single one — so `the-digest-has-an-error-bar`'s published collision rates are not a quality metric but
  the premise of that derivation.
- Chirality is data beside the graph: `Hand`, `Oriented`, `or-mirror`, `Meso`, and `meso-self-mirror`,
  which proves that for a meso compound every relabelling-invariant observation of the orientation reads
  the same on the molecule and on its mirror image. `OrAuto` and `OrOrbit` are the oriented molecule's
  automorphisms and orbits, and `or-orbit-refines` proves the refinement that `nmr-orbits` needs.
- `AtomMap` is mass balance stated without counting: a relabelling of the reactant atoms onto the product
  atoms with its inverse, preserving each atom's element. `am-after-auto` and `am-before-auto` give the
  action of both molecules' automorphism groups on the atom maps, so `reaction-degeneracy` is not a
  remark about multiplicity but the statement that a stored map is a representative of an orbit with the
  orbit discarded.
- `Scope` is a claim's coverage as a type family over molecules, and `scope-respects` proves that no scope
  distinguishes identical molecules — `markush` and `regulatory-identity` as a theorem about what a claim
  can possibly cover.
- The three identities are separated by two refutations rather than by assertion. `Solid` is a molecule
  with the space group assigned to its crystal; `PolymorphPair` is one molecule, two solids, two space
  groups; and `polymorph-not-determined` derives from one such pair that molecular identity does not
  determine the solid. `Substance` is what a regulator has — a scope over molecules and a provenance —
  `ProvenanceCollision` is two substances of one provenance differing on a molecule, and
  `provenance-not-identity` derives from one that provenance does not determine the substance. Each
  refutation needs a single inhabitant of the pair type, and the field has published those inhabitants:
  ritonavir Form II, and the Commission's jointly registered anode copper from different sources.
- The observation layer is written as well, and it is the piece that makes this a knowledge graph rather
  than a chemical database. `Report` holds the molecule observed, the proposition the number rests on —
  as a type, with an inhabitant of it — and the value; `report-retracted` proves that refuting the warrant
  refutes the report, so a report whose warrant has fallen is an absurdity rather than a record with a
  flag on it. `Derived` holds the reports a quantity was computed from, indexed by whatever indexes them,
  together with the function that computes it, and `der-retracted` proves that refuting any one of those
  warrants refutes the quantity. Nothing is recomputed to know this and nothing is marked stale: the
  dependency carries it, which is exactly what the computed-property databases cannot state and why a
  correction there is a new release rather than a retraction.
- The worked case is written and both of its statements are proved, which is the demonstration's kernel
  rather than its table. A central atom carries two hydrogens and one other substituent; the elements,
  the bonds (a function of which atom is the centre), the relabelling that exchanges the two hydrogens,
  and its preservation of element and bond are all written out. `at-h-one-orbit` proves the two hydrogens
  lie in one orbit of the bond graph. With an orientation that differs at the two of them — what a second
  centre elsewhere in a real molecule imposes — `at-h-not-one-or-orbit` proves they lie in no orbit of the
  oriented molecule. One molecule, two relations, two theorems: the graph-only count predicts one
  resonance here and the oriented count predicts two. What remains for the table is scale and published
  spectra, not the argument.
- The measurement's own identity is written too, because the affinity record's largest defect turned out
  to be that it has none. `Measured` carries the event that produced a report beside the report;
  `Distinct` is the hypothesis every statistic over an aggregate needs — that the family is injective on
  events; `DoubleCount` is two places in a family holding one event; and `double-count-not-distinct`
  refutes the hypothesis from a single one. That is `affinity-uncertainty`'s 90% as a type. The mixing of
  pKi with pIC₅₀ needs no new definition: `Derived I V` aggregates reports of one value type, so mixing
  two kinds of measurement requires first erasing the distinction between them, which is what the
  databases do by storing both as a number.
- The pharmacology layer is written on top of it. `BindClaim` holds an oriented molecule, a target, a
  measurement with its event and warrant, and the proof that the measurement was of this molecule;
  `bind-transport` carries a claim along identity of oriented molecules, using the path. The claim is
  about the oriented molecule because the two enantiomers of a drug are two claims. The target is an
  opaque identifier, deliberately: a protein's identity is not a molecular graph, and `biologics` says
  why none will do. `Interconv`, `ic-within` and the thalidomide instance (`td-inv`, `td-one-in-a-day`,
  `td-two-in-ten-minutes`) make the identification of forms depend on the observation window, as
  computed data. Together they say which inferences the pharmacology record is entitled to: transport
  along a path, yes; a digest collision, no (`collision-not-injective`); a relation that does not
  compose, no (`non-transitive-not-identity`). The record makes all three.
- Two statements about control and evidence close it. `BScope` is a control instrument in the form it
  takes — a yes or no on each molecule, which is what a scheduled structural class and a Markush claim
  both are; `AffinitySettles` is what would have to hold for such an instrument to control anything, that
  the affinity settles the membership; `Evasion` is two claims of one affinity with one molecule inside
  the class and one outside; and `evasion-refutes` derives the refutation from a single one. That is
  `substantially-similar` and `scheduling-by-structure` as a theorem. And on evidence: `vacuous-report`
  shows a report can always be made, for any molecule and any value, by taking the warrant to be the
  proposition that holds trivially — so the existence of a record is no evidence, which is exactly what a
  fabricated structure is. `Informative` says what makes a family of warrants worth anything, that there
  is a claim it refuses, and `unit-warrant-not-informative` proves the trivial warrant refuses nothing.
- Two closures and one named next step. `at-map-id` and `at-map-swap` are both atom maps of the worked
  molecule to itself and `at-maps-differ` proves they are different maps, so `reaction-degeneracy` is
  concrete: a record storing one atom map is storing a choice, and here the orbit has two elements and the
  record has room for one. `ic-respects` joins the interconversion data to the tautomer carrier: over the
  forms an observation window identifies, every property of the carrier agrees, so a quantity that differs
  between two fast-interconverting forms cannot be stated of the substance under that observation at all —
  not by convention but because no such function exists. And the enantiotopic case is
  derived, which was the sharpest test this document set itself. `Cyc` is the arrangement at a tetrahedral
  atom — points are triples of neighbours, paths are the three-cycles, so two arrangements are equal
  exactly when they are rotations of one another — and `cyc-sign` is a sign on the arrangements
  themselves, defined on the points and carried along the rotation paths by `sgn-rot`, which is what makes
  it a function of a configuration rather than of a drawing. On that: `cyc-swap-differs` proves that
  exchanging the two hydrogens of a methylene group next to a stereocentre is not a rotation, so it is not
  an automorphism of the molecule with its configuration, and the two positions are distinct —
  diastereotopicity derived from the configuration instead of assigned to the atoms. `cyc-mirror-swap-same`
  proves that the exchange composed with the reflection is a rotation, by the path the type carries, so a
  medium admitting reflections identifies the two positions again: they are enantiotopic. With
  `at-h-one-orbit`, that is three groups and three verdicts on one molecule — the bond graph identifies
  the pair, the configuration separates it, reflection identifies it again — and the medium, not the
  molecule, decides which applies. The textbook's three cases are now three theorems. And the
  arrangements are joined to the molecule: `cyc-map` relabels an arrangement, carrying its rotation paths
  with it; `Stereo` is a molecule with the arrangement at each atom, which is the bond graph and the
  stereochemistry as data of the same kind rather than descriptors bolted onto a string; `StAuto` is an
  automorphism that carries each arrangement to the arrangement at the atom it is sent to, with equality
  taken in `Cyc`, so a relabelling that reverses an arrangement is not one of them; and
  `st-orbit-refines` proves that its orbits refine the graph's. The three verdicts are properties of one
  object.
- Four of the field's standing problems are now statements in it rather than difficulties around it.
  `HMol` is bonding as it is — atoms, a type of bonds, the atoms each bond is incident on, the electron
  count — with `TwoCentred` the property the standard model enforces, `hmol-of-moleq` the embedding of the
  standard representation that loses nothing, `hmol-two-centred` the proof that everything the embedding
  produces has that property, `bridge` one B–H–B bridge of diborane as a single bond on three atoms, and
  `bridge-not-two-centred` and `three-centre-not-two-centred` the proof that no such object is in the
  image: the inorganic and organometallic boundary as a fact about carriers (`organometallics`).
  `taut-no-lift` settles the tautomer standard: a digest differing across one admissible transfer is not
  the restriction of any function on the substance (`tautomers`). `Kek`, `kek-conv`, `kek-one-substance`
  and `kek-no-distinguishing-property` put aromaticity where it belongs, as an interconversion faster than
  any observation, with no property of the carrier distinguishing the two Kekulé structures. `Mix` with
  `mix-frac-differs` makes a mixture its proportions, so provenance does not determine a UVCB
  (`registrant-practice`).
- The inference layer is written as well, because every regulatory conclusion is a composition of
  transports. `HazardDetermined` states the claim a read-across adaptation makes, `ra-transports` carries
  it, `ra-via-property` is the group argument that works — the hazard as a function of a measured property
  rather than of the structure — `TransfersOn` is the scope on which a model system stands for the human,
